|~ `::tag`, the kind of a tag name, and what is declared under it: the
   refusal of a payload of another kind, the verbs that turn a tag name into a
   string and a keyword, and `toTag`, which answers the tag itself.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:tag
  |~~ A tag names a kind, and a value carries its kind as the tag over
      it: `[1 2]` is of `::vec`, `::Box[1 2]` a vector under `::Box`.
      Taken alone, `::Box` is a value of this kind, the name a query
      asks about the kind: `::vec | doc` reads its page and
      `::vec | manifest` lists what lies under it, and `tag` answers
      the tag of any value, `[1 2] | tag` answering `::vec`.

      It is written `::` and a name, a slash joining names into an
      address, `::vec/count`; a tag that touches a payload puts the
      payload under it, which ::link~(::tagged) tells. A label is a
      kind declared under a name, by the chain that builds it from
      ::link~(::kind) or by its page alone, and its tag is the
      address of that name; a tag nothing declares is a kind of identity,
      which checks nothing and lays itself over the value. Tags rank after
      keywords and before paths, and JSON writes a tag as its literal,
      `"::Box"`.
      ::snippet~(::host | kinds) lists the kinds the scope reads, and
      ::snippet~(::Box::Crate{:width 2} | tag) answers the outer tag.
      ::link~(::qlang/values)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ A tag name, read as itself. ~~| ::tag
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ `::tag` reads its payload as the tag name it is; a value's own
            tag is read by `tag`.
        ~~|
    | proves :isATag
        |~~ A tag name is a value of `::tag`. ~~|
        ~(::Box | tag | eq ::tag)
    | proves :namesAPage
        |~~ The tag of a kind names its page. ~~|
        ~(5 | tag | doc | tag | eq ::doc)
    | proves :namesNothingUndeclared
        |~~ A tag no declaration answers names no record. ~~|
        ~(::Unbound[1] | tag | binding !| tag | eq ::any/binding/UnknownNameError)
    | proves :readsATagNameAsItself
        |~~ `::tag` over a tag name is that name. ~~|
        ~(::tag::Box | eq ::Box)
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesAKeyword
        |~~ A keyword payload is refused. ~~|
        ~(::tag:k !| get [~(tag) ~(found | tag)] | eq [::tag/PayloadKindNotTakenError ::keyword]);

:tag/toString
  |~~ Answers the name of the tag as a string, `::vec | toString`
      answering `"vec"`, so a kind joins text. `toTag` turns the name
      back into the tag.
      ::link~(::string/toTag)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The name of the tag, a string. ~~| ::string
    | proves :answersTheName
        |~~ A tag answers its name. ~~|
        ~([::vec ::number/add] | map ~toString | eq ["vec" "number/add"])
    | impl ::builtin{};

:tag/toKeyword
  |~~ Answers the keyword of the tag's name, `::Box | toKeyword`
      answering `:Box`, as `groupBy ~(tag)` files values by their kinds.
      `toTag` turns the keyword back into the tag.
      ::link~(::keyword/toTag)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The keyword of the tag's name. ~~| ::keyword
    | proves :readsBack
        |~~ A tag turned into its keyword turns back into itself. ~~|
        ~(::Box | toKeyword | toTag | eq ::Box)
    | impl ::builtin{};

:tag/toTag
  |~~ Answers the tag itself, so `map ~toTag` turns names and tags into
      tags, `["vec" :Box ::map] | map ~toTag` answering
      `[::vec ::Box ::map]`.
      ::link~(::string/toTag)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The tag itself. ~~| ::tag
    | proves :answersItself
        |~~ A tag answers itself, so names and tags turn into tags. ~~|
        ~(["vec" :Box ::map] | map ~toTag | eq [::vec ::Box ::map])
    | impl ::builtin{};

